```

The time domain retrieval and tick estimation logic is duplicated between the bottom X axis (lines 656-668) and top X axis (lines 718-724). Consider extracting this validation logic into a reusable helper function to improve maintainability and reduce code duplication.

For example:
```javascript
function shouldApplyCustomTicks(timeScale, every, interval) {
  const domain = timeScale.domain();
  const estimatedTicks = getEstimatedTickCount(domain[0], domain[1], every, interval);

  if (estimatedTicks > MAX_TICK_COUNT) {
    log.warn(
      `The tick interval "${every}${interval}" would generate ${estimatedTicks} ticks, ` +
        `which exceeds the maximum allowed (${MAX_TICK_COUNT}). ` +
        `This may indicate an invalid date or time range. Skipping custom tick interval.`
    );
    return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```
