The comment on lines 304-307 states "if dayjs strict parsing fails - throws an error" but the code doesn't actually throw an error at this point. The error is only thrown later (line 325) after additional validation checks. The comment should be clarified to indicate that for non-timestamp formats, the code will eventually throw an error if the fallback `new Date(str)` parsing also fails.
```suggestion
